  "practice": [
    "Say ত three times with the tongue near the teeth: tô, tô, tô.",
    "Practice the vowel forms: ত (tô), তা (ta), তি (ti), তী (ti), তু (tu), তূ (tu), তে (te), তৈ (toi), তো (to), and তৌ (tou).",
    "Read the common combinations aloud: ত + া = তা as in তারা, ত + ি = তি as in তিন, ত + ী = তী as in তীব্র, ত + ু = তু as in তুমি, ত + ে = তে as in তেল, ত + ৈ = তৈ as in তৈরি, and ত + ো = তো as in তোমার.",
    "Practice the related time words এখন, তখন, and কখন: now, then, and when.",
    "Practice the -তে infinitive pattern with করতে, যেতে, খেতে, বলতে, দেখতে, জানতে, থাকতে, and শিখতে.",
    "Contrast ত and থ with your hand near your mouth: ত releases little air; থ releases a noticeable puff.",
    "Find ত inside এটা, সেটা, কত, কথা, ভিতরে, রাতে, সাথে, নতুন, প্রথম, বন্ধু, and ভালোবাসতে.",
    "Use তুমি, তোমার, তারা, তাহলে, তাই, তখন, তিন, টাকা, তাড়াতাড়ি, তৈরি, and তেল as quick reading anchors.",
    "Recognize these phrases instantly: তুমি কেমন আছো, তোমার নাম কী, তাহলে চলো, তাড়াতাড়ি করো, and তুমি তৈরি."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ত is one of the most common Bangla consonants. It is called দন্ত্য ত (dôntyo tô) and is pronounced with the tongue near the teeth.",
    "ত is an unaspirated dental t. Its partner থ uses a similar tongue position with an extra puff of air.",
    "তুমি is the normal familiar-polite form of you. তোমার means your, তোমাকে means you or to you, and তোমাদের addresses or refers to more than one person.",
    "The time words এখন, তখন, and কখন form a useful visual set: now, then, and when.",
    "তাহলে means then or in that case, while তাই means so, therefore, or that's why.",
    "The ending -তে appears in many useful infinitive forms, including করতে, যেতে, খেতে, বলতে, দেখতে, জানতে, থাকতে, and শিখতে.",
    "Best ত words to memorize include তুমি, তোমার, তোমাকে, তারা, তাদের, তাকে, তাহলে, তাই, তখন, তিন, টাকা, তাড়াতাড়ি, তারিখ, তাজা, তৈরি, তেল, তোলা, তুলনা, তথ্য, তদন্ত, and ত্বক."
  ]
}
